  "slug": "genetic-effects-1a8b",
  "summary": "Preprints on IBD, T2D, osteoarthritis and alcohol use disorder go beyond expression QTLs to splicing, allelic chromatin, MPRA and enhancer-gene benchmarks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is assigning disease-associated noncoding variants to effector genes in relevant tissues or cell types, increasingly beyond total transcript abundance. Joint colon eQTL and sQTL mapping in 1,149 IBD samples finds GWAS-colocalized expression and splicing effects implicating NMD and immune pathways. Colocalization of 338 fine-mapped T2D signals with adipose expression, splicing and transcript usage identifies RNA features missed by expression alone. Pangenome genotyping of 645,680 structural variants in CARTaGENE yields 103 SV-eQTLs. Mechanistic follow-up appears at individual loci: MPRA and CRISPR perturbation in chondrocytes link rs1895062 to PAPPA, and microglial allele-specific accessibility shows rs7307261 alters ETS-factor binding. Methods target the enhancer-gene step directly: CREMAP adjusts latent factors before peak-gene testing in single-cell multiome data, E2GScore benchmarks sequence-to-function models, and EPIC2 maps traits to cell types from single-cell accessibility. The IGVF Catalog integrates 657 datasets as shared infrastructure.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
